examples.question_text:
A parabola has $x$-intercepts at $x=-2$ and $x=5$. Write its equation in factored form if:
(a) it is monic;
(b) the coefficient of $x^2$ is $4$.

Find the equation of the parabola shown in vertex form.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.65cm,y=0.4cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[<->,black] (-1.5,0)--(5.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-4)--(0,6.5) node[above] {$y$};
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$O$};
\draw[curveBlue,thick,<->,domain=-0.1:4.1,samples=90] plot (\x,{-2*(\x-2)*(\x-2)+6});
\fill[black] (2,6) circle (2pt);
\fill[black] (0,-2) circle (2pt);
\node[above] at (2,6) {$(2,6)$};
\node[left] at (0,-2) {$(0,-2)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the equation of the parabola shown in factored form.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.6cm,y=0.3cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[<->,black] (-5.5,0)--(3.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-10)--(0,5) node[above] {$y$};
\node[above right] at (0,0) {$O$};
\draw[curveBlue,thick,<->,domain=-4.7:2.7,samples=90] plot (\x,{(\x+4)*(\x-2)});
\fill[black] (-4,0) circle (2pt);
\fill[black] (2,0) circle (2pt);
\fill[black] (0,-8) circle (2pt);
\node[above left] at (-4,0) {$-4$};
\node[above right] at (2,0) {$2$};
\node[right] at (0,-8) {$(0,-8)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
